            <ArticleTitle>Protruding left intercostal mass after left ventricular aneurysmectomy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>657-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In this report we summarize a case of myocardial infarction that developed an apical ventricular aneurysm, which was surgically removed to re-expand and reappear as a pulsating chest wall mass 16 years later.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
